# The yarn.lock located at the root of the repository is only here to hint
# Heroku that Yarn should be used to build and run the project. This file is
# not used to track dependencies and must thus be left empty otherwise it
# disturbes Yarn when run on Heroku. Dependencies are tracked by the
# corresponding yarn.lock files found on workspaces sub-directories.
yarn.lock
